> Newbie Question: Identification

Price-id is key.  Find a general store, drop all your unidentified 
stuff, and see how much the shopkeeper will offer.  Now compare to the 
prices listed in your favorite spoilers.  (Drop something you know the 
cost of to get a baseline.)

Some of the time, the shopkeeper will offer 25% less than he usually 
does; so you may have to drop things several time to distinguish cost-60 
scrolls from cost-80 scrolls, and cost-150 potions/rings from cost-200 
potions/rings.

Once you've got the price of everything, you can more efficiently decide 
what you are willing to try, and what you are willing to save until you 
can identify it with an identify scroll (which is, incidentally, 
particularly easy to price-id).

This method isn't very useful for gems, but then gems aren't very useful 
anyway.  If you haven't maxed your Luck, find a co-aligned unicorn and 
throw #named gems at it.

Price-id is also very good at picking out quickly what weapons and armor 
have come pre-enchanted.

